I waited till the November patch before playing this game.  I can't speak for what performance would have been like on my pc prior to this. All I know is that I haven't experienced any severe pc problems that many have. I'm truly sorry for those who are having them as at it's core, Rocksteady has scored their crowning achievement with Arkham Knight.
Pros:
Very well written. In my opinion, the most flushed out story of the Arkham game franchise;
Stunning graphics though the AA could be better;
Nice Easter eggs spread throughout the game and some real surprises throughout;
Rocksteady has managed to breathe new life in features from the previous games.
Cons:
The Batmobile is ok once you get use to it but I think it's overused. I would have been happier with the game overall if there was less of the "arcade experience" with the Batmobile.
Stunning graphics though the AA could be better. I believe the AA in this game is post processing, similar to the AA found in "Alien Isolation" (another great game BTW).
All in all, if your pc has the horsepower, this game is a lotta fun.  Rocksteady has put a lot of heart and soul into making this story and I hope whatever is next for them is as exciting. Step beyond the plethora of negativity about this game and fire up Arkham Knight.

