Honestly, the game is overall great. Cinematic quality effects, a large choice of weapondry, vast amounts of enemies. Oh, and perhaps slo-mo kills while in multiplayer that fits well. Overall, I enjoy it, i've been able to play with each of the six classes so far in to get a feeling of them, and how they are independent and have their own important roles. I've only found one little issue with the game... Well, it's not so little, its game breaking, and I mean literally! The game has some serious compatibility issues, and usually take a few months to have ironed out. For example, right now it is saying
but as soon as I press okay, it closes. I've looked for ways to solve this for hours, and the only one(
) is to reinstall steam itself, which has hundreds of gigabytes of information. I know you may think I am over reacting and such, but I've also had another time when I was unable to play for about relatively 3 months due to my little steam icon turning green and then blue again, without launching it. Once again, I also looked for hours for a solution, all of which that failed.

This is simply the best PC game ever made.
Reasons:
-best story in a video game;
-one of the best graphic engines ever seen (even at 2014 standards) which runs more than smoothly. By the way, this game has the best human facial movements out there (I think only LA Noire is better at this).
-funny and entertaining;
-great controls and handling;
-lasting appeal (this is my 3rd replay);
-pretty long campaign (great value): something that we don't see anymore in modern videogames.

Important things you should know before you decide whether to buy this game:
1. Even after 4 month of 'fixing' work from WB brothers, this game still has serious problems, which reminds me of Mortal Kombat X, also a piece of crap. And some guy from WB has just said, you need at least 12 GB RAM to 'run this game smoothly';
2. It's true that WB will offer you free copies of games from Batman Library. For those who are new to Batman game,  pls notice, you can get them withing 10 bucks in any other website of key retailers, rather than pay more than 40 bucks to buy this game on steam and get them for free. Of course, if you are an old fan of Batman series who have already bought every game of its kind, in return to your loyalty and patience, you will get nothing! Isn't it amazing? Cheers!;
3. Game itself, except for terrible optimization, is great. The whole story line is fascinating and new Batmobile is of great fun.  I would suggest you to buy a key from any other key retailers with much lower price to experience the game. ( I got mine withing 15 bucks).
And some words for WB: You guys have really wasted this wonderful game on PC. It should have been one of the best games this year, but now... Batman is dead for sure.

