Wow, what a fun game! I was lucky enough for the 1st patch to make to game play amazingly. Arkham is one of my favorite game series and this one did not disapoint me at all.
Pros:
- Fun engaging story as the previous ones
- Amazing visuals!
- Such a fun diverse gameplay!
- Seamless gameplay from gliding in the sky to jumping in the batmobile to taking down tanks, back to gliding to taking down a drone, to beating up thugs in the streets, to etc, etc, (this is increadible and so much fun!);
- This is the only game that I try to complete 100% while enjoying every single side missions (compared to AC series or GTA, which can be frustrating or simply boring);
- It's also a rare game where if I lose, I don't feel cheated by the AI or the bad design of the game, it just encourages me to get better at the combat and predator skills;
- The batmobile is a nice addition. It doesn't feel too forced since there is a lot of non-batmobile missions and gameplay;
Season Pass:  I personnaly really enjoyed the season pass (got it on sale). Even if the season pass missions were short, they were many and very enjoyable. The racing tracks were also really fun!
Cons:
- The PC port problem was quite disapointing and ridiculous... Too many publishers put out broken games... It's too bad, mostly after I thought GTAV had started a good trend of taking the time to make proper and good PC version of a game...  (However, the game is still a blast and I can't wait to play the DLCs!)
Much recommended for anyone who likes the series and this type of game.

